stomer would like to  collect data in iron mobility mode  then we would use the mobile ion  software  to control the system and to collect  that data  but once the data is collected we  support conversion to the standard.d  format and at that point you're able to  pull the data  into the full suite of agile tools that  support  eye mobility mass spec data  thank you for that we have time for one  more question which qtop models will be  supported  with this system  yep so currently we've targeted  designing  towards the 6545 the 6545  xt and the 6546  models  thank you so much dr klein dr debord  thank you for your presentation today  would you like to provide any final  comments for our audience members before  we close  well um you know i again like to thank  agilent for this opportunity  to share our work uh and also the  viewers for their their time and their  interest  at mobile mobileline we're very excited  about the future of slim  and we look forward you know we didn't  mention it in the presentation but we're  targeting a commercial  product release in 2021  the data that you've seen is coming off  of our prototype and beta systems  but we're working towards getting that  out into  um you know the broader community  and so hopefully we'll be able to join  together next year for asms in  philadelphia  in person this time and i look forward  to sharing  some more of the incredible work that  our team and our collaborators are doing  with slim  and we feel that both on the development  side and on  the application side we've really only  scratched the surface  of what's possible with this  revolutionary technology  and so i encourage anybody that's  interested in learning more  about slim or what it might be able to  do in your application  that you'd reach out to us and we would  love to talk to you about it  thank you so much and dr klein did you  want to add anything  i would like to thank the audience for  participating in  agilent's virtual mass spectacular  events so thank you a lot for your  participation  and uh i'm sure that you are equally  excited about  the data that daniel presented the  capabilities that  the slim device can offer on agilent's  skeutoff and  with that i'm really excited to see this  moving forward into the next phase  and again thank you for a participation  in the webinar  thank you and john thank you again both  of you for your time  for your important research and before  we go i want to thank the audience for  joining us today and for their  interesting questions  questions we did not have time for today  and those submitted  during the on-demand period will be  addressed by the speaker  via the contact information you provided  at the time of registration  and this webcast can be viewed on demand  through june  of 2021. until next time  take care and be safe bye

